-
-Current proven associations appear first. Superseded and applicability-unknown rows remain
-separately inspectable. Legacy absence cannot manufacture current provenance. Counts alone
-never establish QA pass or clean completion. Old clients may omit these additive projections;
-an older executing Core is not qualified for the new semantics.
-
-The complete Inspect definition stays within 5,000 bytes, each write definition within 8,192,
-and all five plus the facade within 24,576. Command input is 64 KiB, referenced material
-128 KiB, and serialized control result 1 MiB. A post-dispatch size/worker failure reports
-uncertainty with the original UUID, not a rollback. Actual source/build/served resource identities,
-rendered locale coverage and native permission/action/teardown observations must be recorded
-separately before whole-flow QA. No weaker-model performance benefit is inferred from unit tests.
